---
import NightPage from '../../layouts/NightPage.astro';
import NightNav from '../../components/layout/NightNav.astro';
import NightFooter from '../../components/layout/NightFooter.astro';
import FigureCanvas from '../../components/ui/FigureCanvas.tsx';
import { AREA, VIEW_NAMES, draftLayout } from '../../figures/kit/legodraft';
import { build } from '../../figures/kit/legoswap';
import { F1 } from '../../figures/kit/legoformula';

// The drawing's text is DOM, set from the same layout the figure draws by, so it lines up.
const layout = draftLayout('rearwing');
const pct = (f: number): string => `${(f * 100).toFixed(2)}%`;
const names = layout.views.map(({ view, rect }) => {
  const top = view === 'side' || view === 'end';
  return { name: VIEW_NAMES[view], x: pct((rect.x0 + rect.x1) / 2), y: pct(top ? rect.y0 : rect.y1), top };
});
const symbol = { x: pct((layout.symbol.x0 + layout.symbol.x1) / 2), y: pct(layout.symbol.y1) };
const pieces = build(F1).length;
const stud = Math.round(layout.sketch.scale * 1000);
const steps = [
  ['Brief', 'Name the object and what makes it read as itself. Pick a scale: one stud is its real width over the studs you can spare.'],
  ['Sketch', 'Find the real proportions and write down where each number came from. Model the real thing in simple solids, not in bricks.'],
  ['Draw', 'Turn the sketch into a first-angle drawing with its dimensions, and read it the way a stranger would.'],
  ['Plan', 'Write the model as shapes a builder knows, and lay them over the sketch to see where they part ways.'],
  ['Pieces', 'If a shape has no piece, add the piece to the catalogue first, from LEGO’s own sizes. Never fake one.'],
  ['Check', 'Swap the shapes for pieces. Nothing may clip, float or sit off the grid, and the check is never bent to pass.'],
  ['Build', 'Mount the model as a figure that builds itself piece by piece, and run the figure audit.'],
  ['Look', 'Read every sheet before the next stage. When something is wrong, go back to the stage that made it.'],
];
const commands = `npm run lego:sheet -- rearwing sketch     # the real part, four views
npm run lego:sheet -- rearwing drawing    # this sheet, on A3
npm run lego:sheet -- rearwing compare    # the plan laid over the sketch
npm run lego:check                        # clipping, floating, off the grid
npm run figure -- lego-f1                 # the build, audited`;
---

<NightPage
  title="Designing in LEGO · Lab · Juan Kok"
  description="How the LEGO models on this site are made: a first-angle engineering drawing of the real part, a plan in shapes checked against it, then pieces, checked before any is drawn."
>
  <NightNav current="lab" />
  <main class="nt-wrap nt-section">
    <header class="lg-head">
      <a href="/lab/">← the lab</a>
      <span>// lab · lego</span>
      <h1>Draw it first.<br />Then build it in LEGO.</h1>
      <p>
        Every LEGO model here starts the way an engineer starts a part. First a drawing of the real thing, in views that each show one face
        true to size. Then a plan in simple shapes, held up against the drawing. Only then does it become bricks, and a script checks every
        brick before one is drawn.
      </p>
      <div class="lg-meta"><span>first-angle projection</span><span>1 stud = {stud} mm</span><span>{pieces} pieces</span></div>
    </header>

    <section class="lg-section" aria-labelledby="lg-drawing">
      <h2 id="lg-drawing"><span>01</span> The drawing</h2>
      <p>
        This is the rear wing the LEGO F1 was built against, drawn to the 2026 rules as reported. It uses first-angle projection, the British
        and European habit. The side elevation is the main view. What you see from the nose sits to its right, and what you see from above sits
        below it. Hidden edges are dashed, the chain line is the centre of the car, and the two coloured marks on the endplates are its lights.
      </p>
      <figure class="lg-sheet">
        <div class="lg-draw" style={`aspect-ratio: ${AREA.w} / ${AREA.h}`}>
          <FigureCanvas client:visible id="lego-drawing" />
          {names.map((n) => <span class:list={['lg-tag', n.top ? 'lg-above' : 'lg-below']} style={`left: ${n.x}; top: ${n.y}`}>{n.name}</span>)}
          {
            layout.dims.map((d) => (
              <span class:list={['lg-dim', d.vertical && 'lg-vertical']} style={`left: ${pct(d.x)}; top: ${pct(d.y)}`}>
                {d.mm}
              </span>
            ))
          }
          <span class="lg-tag lg-below" style={`left: ${symbol.x}; top: ${symbol.y}`}>First angle</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lg-foot">
          <ol class="lg-notes">
            <li>Dimensions in mm, full size. One stud is {stud} mm of the real car and 8 mm in LEGO.</li>
            <li>Hidden edges dashed, centre lines chain-dotted, lights in the signal colour.</li>
            <li>Proportions from the rules as reported. No photograph was traced.</li>
          </ol>
          <dl class="lg-block">
            <div class="lg-title"><dt>Title</dt><dd>{layout.sketch.title}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Drawing no.</dt><dd>JS-LEGO-REARWING-01</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Scale (A3)</dt><dd>1:{layout.scale}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Projection</dt><dd>First angle</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Drawn</dt><dd>Claude</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Date</dt><dd>{layout.sketch.drawn}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Units</dt><dd>mm</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="lg-aside">
        Read the projection symbol first. In third angle, the American habit, the same drawing puts the plan above the side elevation and the
        nose view on its left. Misread it and the part comes back mirrored.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="lg-section" aria-labelledby="lg-build">
      <h2 id="lg-build"><span>02</span> The build</h2>
      <p>
        The drawing is read in studs. The wing is planned as shapes a builder knows (plates, tiles, brackets turned on their side, flaps on
        hinges), laid over the drawing to compare, then swapped into pieces. The checks refuse anything that clips, floats or sits off the
        grid. Below is the whole car, built and taken apart in the order a person would.
      </p>
      <div class="lg-stage"><FigureCanvas client:visible id="lego-f1" /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="lg-section" aria-labelledby="lg-playbook">
      <h2 id="lg-playbook"><span>03</span> The playbook</h2>
      <p>The same eight steps for anything, a car or a building. Each one ends with its sheet read before the next starts.</p>
      <ol class="lg-steps">
        {
          steps.map(([name, text]) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{name}</strong>
              <span>{text}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <div class="lg-terminal">
        <div class="lg-terminal-bar"><span class="lg-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>astro/ · the sheets</span></div>
        <pre tabindex="0"><code>{commands}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <NightFooter />
</NightPage>

<style>
  .lg-head,
  .lg-section > p,
  .lg-section > h2 {
    max-width: var(--nt-measure);
  }
  .lg-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--hf-space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--hf-space-16);
  }
  .lg-head > a,
  .lg-head > span,
  .lg-meta,
  .lg-section h2 span {
    font: var(--nt-fs-meta) / var(--nt-lh-body) var(--nt-mono);
  }
  .lg-head > a {
    color: var(--nt-ink-muted);
  }
  .lg-head > span,
  .lg-section h2 span {
    color: var(--nt-signal-text);
  }
  .lg-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--nt-display);
    font-size: var(--nt-fs-h1);
    letter-spacing: var(--nt-tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--nt-lh-heading);
  }
  .lg-head p,
  .lg-section > p {
    color: var(--nt-ink-soft);
  }
  .lg-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--hf-space-3) var(--hf-space-6);
    color: var(--nt-ink-muted);
  }
  .lg-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--hf-space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--hf-space-16);
  }
  .lg-section h2 {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--hf-space-4);
    align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--nt-display);
    font-size: var(--nt-fs-h3);
    color: var(--nt-ink-strong);
  }
  .lg-sheet {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--nt-line-3);
    padding: var(--hf-space-4);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .lg-draw {
    position: relative;
  }
  .lg-tag,
  .lg-dim {
    position: absolute;
    font-family: var(--nt-mono);
    font-size: min(var(--nt-fs-caption), 2.2cqw);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--nt-ink-2);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .lg-above {
    transform: translate(-50%, -160%);
  }
  .lg-below {
    transform: translate(-50%, 50%);
  }
  .lg-dim {
    transform: translate(-50%, -120%);
  }
  .lg-dim.lg-vertical {
    transform: translate(-120%, -50%) rotate(-90deg) translateY(-50%);
    transform-origin: 100% 50%;
  }
  .lg-foot {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(0, 1.4fr);
    gap: var(--hf-space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--nt-line-3);
    padding-top: var(--hf-space-4);
  }
  .lg-notes {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--hf-space-5);
    font: var(--nt-fs-caption) / var(--nt-lh-body) var(--nt-mono);
    color: var(--nt-ink-muted);
  }
  .lg-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--nt-line-3);
  }
  .lg-block > div {
    padding: var(--hf-space-2) var(--hf-space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--nt-line-2);
  }
  .lg-block .lg-title {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .lg-block dt {
    font: var(--nt-fs-caption) var(--nt-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--nt-ink-muted);
  }
  .lg-block dd {
    margin: 0;
    font: var(--nt-fs-small) var(--nt-mono);
    color: var(--nt-ink);
  }
  .lg-block .lg-title dd {
    font-size: var(--nt-fs-h5);
  }
  .lg-aside {
    font-size: var(--nt-fs-small);
  }
  .lg-stage {
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  }
  .lg-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, var(--nt-card-min)), 1fr));
    gap: var(--hf-space-6);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .lg-steps li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--hf-space-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--nt-line-3);
    padding-top: var(--hf-space-3);
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .lg-steps strong::before {
    content: '0' counter(step) ' · ';
    font: var(--nt-fs-meta) var(--nt-mono);
    color: var(--nt-signal-text);
  }
  .lg-steps strong {
    font-family: var(--nt-display);
    color: var(--nt-ink-strong);
  }
  .lg-steps span {
    font-size: var(--nt-fs-small);
    color: var(--nt-ink-soft);
  }
  .lg-terminal {
    border: 1px solid var(--nt-code-line);
    background: var(--nt-code-ground);
  }
  .lg-terminal-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--hf-space-4);
    padding: var(--hf-space-3) var(--hf-space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--nt-code-line);
    font: var(--nt-fs-caption) var(--nt-mono);
    color: var(--nt-code-muted);
  }
  .lg-dots {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--hf-space-2);
  }
  .lg-dots i {
    width: var(--hf-space-3);
    height: var(--hf-space-3);
    border-radius: var(--hf-radius-pill);
    background: var(--nt-term-red);
  }
  .lg-dots i:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--nt-term-amber);
  }
  .lg-dots i:nth-child(3) {
    background: var(--nt-term-green);
  }
  .lg-terminal pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--hf-space-5);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font: var(--nt-fs-small) / var(--nt-lh-body) var(--nt-mono);
    color: var(--nt-code-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .lg-foot {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
